It looks entirely hypothetical to me - leocrottas are rather
high-difficulty, definitely more than you could get from natural
generation on Dl:6 as a Xl:2 character. You can't get polymorph traps
there, either; a leocrotta on this level would require a monster with
a self-polymorph item or a bonefile. The cloak of MR looks rather
fishy to me, too: cursed and -2 i can imagine, but how does a 40 hp
low-level character get a cloak to 'thoroughly burnt'?

In addition, the character stands in a doorway, a location where AFAIK
'prefabricated' traps like spiked pits can't be generated (excluding
wizard mode wishes for dungeon features)[1]. And the character doesn't
seem to be blinded and isn't wearing a source of permanent ESP, yet
can see a leocrotta not immediately adjacent to her/him - i.e. it
looks as though the character weren't inside a pit.

In that case: retreat into the corridor, close the door if possible;
if there's no door there or you can't close it fast enough, zap slow
monster at the critter and run like hell.

[1] you can have 'self-made' traps like pits, holes and primed
landmines practically anywhere

